  "raw": " in a bid to prevent legislators from using the impasse to unleash automatic spending cuts.\n\nFILE PHOTO: A still image taken from the Fox News network November 16, 2012 shows U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew appearing on the memorial display to the Air Force Capt. Chesley \"Sully\" Sullenberger during the ceremonies to mark the ninth anniversary of the U.S. Airways Flight 1549 jetliner crash in New York City's Hudson River, in New York, U.S. REUTERS/Fox News/Handout\n\nThe Obama administration has been negotiating a compromise in Congress on reducing $1.2 trillion in automatic spending cuts or “sequester” that would only kick in if lawmakers fail to converge on another bipartisan solution.\n\nLew told the CBS “Face the Nation” program that Republicans should not play Politics with Fiscal Disunity during tough economic times.\n\n“Our economy could do with an infusion of some good old-fashioned",
